
# =============================================================================
# Per-Row GO:BP ORA on Reversal Leading Edges -- single self-contained script
# (parallel, restartable, progress bar) -- suitable for one R Markdown chunk.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analysis (unchanged): per row, GO:BP enrichGO(keyType="ENSEMBL"), human,
#   p<0.05 AND q<0.05, universe = that row's drug-signature gene set.
#
# Behaviour:
#   * Runs across (detectCores() - 2) workers via furrr.
#   * Each row writes its own part files to LOCAL scratch the moment it finishes
#     (tidy CSV + raw enrichResult rds), with the done-flag written LAST so its
#     presence guarantees the data is on disk.
#   * RESTARTABLE: rerun the chunk after any interruption -> rows already carrying
#     a done-flag are skipped, and the run resumes where it stopped.
#   * Live progress via progressr (a bar that aggregates across workers).
#   * At the end (once all rows are done) it reassembles the parts into the three
#     final OneDrive outputs: tidy CSV, combined rds, diagnostic log.
#
# Just re-run the whole chunk if it ever stops; it is safe and idempotent.
# =============================================================================

